   "title": "Protein or blood in the urine: is it BENIGN, the GLOMERULUS, or the urinary TRACT?",
   "lines": [
    "for many kidney diseases, the AMOUNT of protein is prognostic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_pr",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 120,
   "w": 732,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "PROTEINURIA: normal < 150 mg/day (albumin < 30)",
   "lines": [
    "1 · QUANTIFY: 24-hour urine (gold standard) or albumin-creatinine ratio (ACR)",
    "• micro: ACR 2–20, dipstick NEGATIVE",
    "• macro: ACR ≥ 20, dipstick +",
    "• dipstick misses light chains: MULTIPLE MYELOMA → serum + urine electrophoresis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_he",
   "x": 817,
   "y": 120,
   "w": 484,
   "h": 114,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "HEMATURIA: ≥ 3 red cells per high-power field",
   "lines": [
    "1 · Ask about ANTICOAGULANTS and bleeding disorders",
    "2 · MICROSCOPY: a dipstick also reacts to hemoglobin + myoglobin; red urine may be beets or phenazopyridine"
   ]
  },
  {
